    "lawCode": "Amd §25, Work Comp L; amd §2, Chap of 2020 (as proposed in S.7210 & A.7579)",
    "lawSection": "Workers' Compensation Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S1298\n\nSPONSOR: SAVINO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the workers' compensation law, in relation to the direct\ndeposit of benefits; and amending a chapter of the laws of 2020 amending\nthe workers' compensation law relating to the direct deposit of bene-\nfits, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S.7210 and A.7579, in\nrelation to the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to make technical changes to Chapter 253 of\nthe Laws of 2020 in order to effectuate the intent of the law.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of the bill would make technical changes to § 25 of the\nWorkers' Compensation Law to clarify the process by which claimants may\nrequest and receive the direct deposit of compensation payments, includ-\ning authorization for the Workers' Compensation Board to promulgate\nregulations for such process. It would also add a new clause to estab-\nlish that the direct deposit of any compensation payment shall not be\nmade if such payment would be in violation of any federal or state law\nor regulation.\n\nSection two of the bill would amend the effective date of the original\nlegislation to July 1, 2021.\n\nSection three of the bill would establish the effective date.\n\n \nDIFFERENCE BETWEEN ORIGINAL AND AMENDED VERSION (IF APPLICABLE):\n\nN/A\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nChapter 253 of the Laws of 2020 mandates that insurance carriers provide\ndirect deposit for compensation payments upon the written request of an\ninjured worker or a person entitled to death benefits under the Workers'\nCompensation Law. This legislation makes technical changes to such law\nin order to authorize the Workers' Compensation Board to promulgate\nregulations for such process and to ensure that such activities do not\nrun afoul of any federal or state laws or regulations.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2020 amending the workers' compensation law\nrelating to the direct deposit of benefits, as proposed in legislative\nbills numbers 5.7210 and A.7579, takes effect.\n",
